 - Return-address disassembly accuracy: a saved RIP in `bt` points to the instruction AFTER `call` (often a loop header or next statement). To confirm the actual call site line, use `dis -rl <ret_addr>` or `dis -s <ret_addr - 1>` rather than attributing the call to the line mapped by bare `dis -s <ret_addr>`.
